0cb800bb-561b-4fad-84e1-a12a38a60b7b	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Find all active tasks", "llm_model": "claude-3-5-sonnet", "use_context": true, "llm_provider": "anthropic"}	{"sql": "SELECT tasks.* FROM tasks LEFT JOIN agent_conversations ON tasks.agent_conversation_id = agent_conversations.id WHERE agent_conversations.ended_at IS NULL LIMIT 100;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves all active tasks from the 'tasks' table. It uses a LEFT JOIN to connect the 'tasks' table with the 'agent_conversations' table based on the 'agent_conversation_id' foreign key. The condition 'WHERE agent_conversations.ended_at IS NULL' filters the results to include only those tasks that are associated with active conversations (i.e., conversations that have not ended). The query limits the results to 100 rows to prevent overwhelming the user with too much data at once. This approach ensures that we only get tasks linked to ongoing conversations, adhering to the requirement for active tasks.", "execution_time_ms": 3855, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	3912	success	\N	ec4fb1e7-fdf1-4522-adc5-6e43acb6d786	0	f	2025-07-26 01:25:19.490258+00	2025-07-26 01:25:23.406736+00
1b6af378-3d48-44e6-8e80-ab755d13aa1b	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Show me the first 3 agents with their names and types", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT agent_name, agent_type FROM agent_conversations ORDER BY created_at LIMIT 3;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query selects the 'agent_name' and 'agent_type' columns from the 'agent_conversations' table. It orders the results by the 'created_at' timestamp to ensure that the first three agents returned are the earliest ones based on when their conversations started. The 'LIMIT 3' clause restricts the output to only the first three records, ensuring that we only retrieve the desired number of agents.", "execution_time_ms": 3116, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	3218	success	\N	acf50aa5-0335-449b-b6d8-004dcec49f0b	0	f	2025-07-26 01:31:14.025053+00	2025-07-26 01:31:17.203494+00
9b54d5b1-df25-46c6-b510-233e9f5a5efc	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Show agent health status for unhealthy agents", "llm_model": "claude-3-5-sonnet", "use_context": true, "llm_provider": "anthropic"}	{"sql": "SELECT a.agent_name, a.agent_type, m.status, m.execution_time_ms, m.created_at FROM agent_conversations a LEFT JOIN mcp_executions m ON a.id = m.agent_conversation_id WHERE m.status = 'unhealthy' LIMIT 100;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves the health status of agents that are marked as 'unhealthy'. It selects the agent's name and type from the 'agent_conversations' table and joins it with the 'mcp_executions' table to get the status and execution time of the agents. The LEFT JOIN ensures that even if there are no corresponding entries in 'mcp_executions', the agent information will still be included. The WHERE clause filters the results to only include those with a status of 'unhealthy'. Finally, a LIMIT of 100 is applied to restrict the number of results returned, which is useful for performance and readability.", "execution_time_ms": 4553, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	4618	success	\N	01f135a6-3b64-496c-a7be-d712cbec6aa3	0	f	2025-07-26 01:25:27.371531+00	2025-07-26 01:25:32.041388+00
3fc737f7-e1cb-441c-b20e-958eac78a068	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Count tasks by status", "llm_model": "claude-3-5-sonnet", "use_context": true, "llm_provider": "anthropic"}	{"sql": "SELECT status, COUNT(*) AS task_count FROM tasks GROUP BY status;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query counts the number of tasks grouped by their status. It selects the 'status' column from the 'tasks' table and uses the COUNT(*) function to count the number of occurrences of each status. The GROUP BY clause is used to aggregate the results based on the 'status' column, ensuring that the count is calculated for each unique status value. This will return a result set with each unique status and the corresponding count of tasks for that status.", "execution_time_ms": 3100, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	3158	success	\N	21c2aa39-5d2a-4a68-88a1-c6ddb703be47	0	f	2025-07-26 01:25:36.939598+00	2025-07-26 01:25:40.101908+00
