03c45416-9f72-46be-a4d3-f8627c644caf	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Show agent health status for unhealthy agents", "llm_model": "claude-3-5-sonnet", "use_context": true, "llm_provider": "anthropic"}	{"sql": "SELECT agent_name, agent_type, COUNT(*) AS unhealthy_count\\nFROM agent_conversations\\nWHERE ended_at IS NOT NULL\\nGROUP BY agent_name, agent_type\\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 0\\nORDER BY unhealthy_count DESC\\nLIMIT 100;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves the health status of agents by counting the number of conversations that have ended (indicating they may be unhealthy). It selects the agent's name and type, and counts the number of conversations where 'ended_at' is not null, which signifies that the conversation has concluded. The results are grouped by 'agent_name' and 'agent_type' to aggregate the counts for each agent. The HAVING clause filters the results to include only those agents with one or more ended conversations, indicating they are unhealthy. The results are ordered by the count of unhealthy conversations in descending order, and a LIMIT of 100 is applied to restrict the output to the top 100 agents based on their unhealthy count.", "execution_time_ms": 4896, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	4957	success	\N	22322bdb-3484-403c-acc6-f24a50652216	0	f	2025-07-26 01:26:40.932958+00	2025-07-26 01:26:45.943032+00
fffa2eb5-a01d-4c3b-b768-269cd22fa1b1	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Count tasks by status", "llm_model": "claude-3-5-sonnet", "use_context": true, "llm_provider": "anthropic"}	{"sql": "SELECT status, COUNT(*) AS task_count FROM tasks GROUP BY status;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query counts the number of tasks grouped by their status. It selects the 'status' column from the 'tasks' table and uses the COUNT(*) function to count the number of occurrences of each status. The GROUP BY clause is used to aggregate the results based on the 'status' column, ensuring that the count is calculated for each unique status value. This will return a result set with each unique status and the corresponding count of tasks in that status.", "execution_time_ms": 3075, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	3148	success	\N	80c6f005-7093-44e7-ac29-8c8ed6ba6cbc	0	f	2025-07-26 01:26:49.832499+00	2025-07-26 01:26:52.984947+00
fdbe10eb-cb17-4bbb-b30d-91dcf71188b6	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Find recent agent interactions with response times", "llm_model": "claude-3-5-sonnet", "use_context": true, "llm_provider": "anthropic"}	{"sql": "SELECT ac.id AS conversation_id, ac.agent_name, ac.agent_type, ac.started_at, ac.ended_at, mcp.execution_time_ms, mcp.created_at AS execution_created_at\\nFROM agent_conversations ac\\nLEFT JOIN mcp_executions mcp ON ac.id = mcp.agent_conversation_id\\nWHERE ac.ended_at IS NULL\\nORDER BY ac.started_at DESC\\nLIMIT 10;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "1. The query selects specific columns from the 'agent_conversations' table (aliased as 'ac') and the 'mcp_executions' table (aliased as 'mcp').\\n2. The selected columns include the conversation ID, agent name, agent type, start and end times of the conversation, execution time of the MCP, and the creation time of the execution.\\n3. A LEFT JOIN is used to combine 'agent_conversations' with 'mcp_executions' on the condition that the 'id' of 'agent_conversations' matches the 'agent_conversation_id' in 'mcp_executions'. This allows us to retrieve execution details even if there are no corresponding MCP executions for some conversations.\\n4. The WHERE clause filters the results to include only active conversations, which are defined as those where 'ended_at' is NULL.\\n5. The results are ordered by the 'started_at' timestamp in descending order, so the most recent conversations appear first.\\n6. Finally, a LIMIT of 10 is applied to restrict the result set to the 10 most recent interactions, ensuring the query remains efficient and manageable.\\n", "execution_time_ms": 7660, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	7734	success	\N	2506abe4-0391-49fe-b69c-70fbf31cc336	0	f	2025-07-26 01:26:53.06166+00	2025-07-26 01:27:00.851859+00
