0f82b29f-b988-4d44-95e8-0c0df73c1ec5	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Show KPI performance against goals", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT mcp.mcp_name, COUNT(mcp.id) AS execution_count, AVG(mcp.execution_time_ms) AS average_execution_time, SUM(CASE WHEN mcp.status = 'success' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS success_count FROM mcp_executions mcp GROUP BY mcp.mcp_name ORDER BY execution_count DESC LIMIT 10;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.85, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves key performance indicators (KPIs) related to the execution of MCPs (Managed Control Processes). It selects the MCP name, counts the total number of executions, calculates the average execution time in milliseconds, and counts the number of successful executions. The data is grouped by MCP name to aggregate the results for each unique MCP. The results are ordered by the execution count in descending order to highlight the most frequently executed MCPs. Finally, a LIMIT clause is applied to return only the top 10 MCPs based on execution count, ensuring the result set is manageable and focused on the most relevant data.", "execution_time_ms": 5457, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	5516	success	\N	cee0100d-cc4e-44ff-9bd9-5b91d986974f	0	f	2025-07-26 01:36:21.534741+00	2025-07-26 01:36:27.104075+00
58510361-7ffa-44b1-b1b2-040d468fe3d0	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Which KPIs are underperforming?", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT mcp_name, COUNT(*) AS execution_count, AVG(execution_time_ms) AS avg_execution_time_ms FROM mcp_executions GROUP BY mcp_name HAVING AVG(execution_time_ms) > (SELECT AVG(execution_time_ms) FROM mcp_executions) ORDER BY avg_execution_time_ms DESC LIMIT 10;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query is designed to identify underperforming Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) based on the average execution time of different MCPs (Managed Control Processes). Here's a breakdown of the query logic:\\n\\n1. **SELECT Clause**: We select the `mcp_name`, the count of executions (`COUNT(*) AS execution_count`), and the average execution time in milliseconds (`AVG(execution_time_ms) AS avg_execution_time_ms`) from the `mcp_executions` table.\\n\\n2. **GROUP BY Clause**: We group the results by `mcp_name` to aggregate the execution counts and average execution times for each MCP.\\n\\n3. **HAVING Clause**: We filter the results to include only those MCPs whose average execution time is greater than the overall average execution time across all MCPs. This is done using a subquery that calculates the overall average execution time.\\n\\n4. **ORDER BY Clause**: The results are ordered in descending order of average execution time, allowing us to see the most underperforming KPIs at the top of the list.\\n\\n5. **LIMIT Clause**: Finally, we limit the results to the top 10 underperforming KPIs to avoid overwhelming output and focus on the most critical cases.\\n\\nThis query effectively highlights which MCPs are taking longer than average to execute, indicating potential areas for improvement in performance.", "execution_time_ms": 7466, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	7563	success	\N	aff46bc5-d55a-4f4b-b9f6-cba5dc79ade4	0	f	2025-07-26 01:36:27.502226+00	2025-07-26 01:36:35.083349+00
