f5169943-4f89-4bc3-9ebc-ca9dbdd785be	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "List all LLM providers and their models, showing total usage count, average execution time, and success rate for each model", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT mcp.tool_name AS llm_provider, mcp.mcp_name AS model, COUNT(mcp.id) AS total_usage_count, AVG(mcp.execution_time_ms) AS average_execution_time, SUM(CASE WHEN mcp.status = 'success' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) * 100.0 / COUNT(mcp.id) AS success_rate FROM mcp_executions mcp GROUP BY mcp.tool_name, mcp.mcp_name ORDER BY llm_provider, model LIMIT 100;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "1. The query selects the tool_name as llm_provider and mcp_name as model from the mcp_executions table. 2. It counts the total number of executions for each model using COUNT(mcp.id) to get total_usage_count. 3. It calculates the average execution time in milliseconds using AVG(mcp.execution_time_ms) for average_execution_time. 4. The success rate is calculated by counting the number of successful executions (where status is 'success') and dividing it by the total count, then multiplying by 100 to get a percentage. 5. The results are grouped by llm_provider and model to ensure each combination is represented once. 6. The results are ordered by llm_provider and model for better readability. 7. A LIMIT clause is added to restrict the result set to 100 rows to prevent overwhelming output.", "execution_time_ms": 6614, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	6684	success	\N	baccb14d-b944-4216-b814-4da0c89b0be9	0	f	2025-07-26 02:12:35.288564+00	2025-07-26 02:12:42.018088+00
