db611584-2fb3-40ae-b1a5-18b9d5af2e68	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Show me sample data from agent_conversations_with_stats table to understand what it contains and what it's used for", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT ac.id, ac.user_id, ac.agent_name, ac.agent_type, ac.started_at, ac.ended_at, ac.last_active_at, ac.created_at, ac.updated_at, COUNT(t.id) AS task_count, COUNT(m.id) AS mcp_execution_count\\nFROM agent_conversations ac\\nLEFT JOIN tasks t ON ac.id = t.agent_conversation_id\\nLEFT JOIN mcp_executions m ON ac.id = m.agent_conversation_id\\nGROUP BY ac.id\\nLIMIT 10;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves sample data from the agent_conversations table along with statistics about related tasks and MCP executions. It selects various columns from the agent_conversations table, including the conversation ID, user ID, agent name, agent type, timestamps for when the conversation started, ended, and was last active, as well as the created and updated timestamps. Additionally, it counts the number of tasks and MCP executions associated with each conversation by using LEFT JOINs to connect the agent_conversations table with the tasks and mcp_executions tables. The results are grouped by the conversation ID to ensure that each conversation appears only once in the output, along with the counts of related records. Finally, a LIMIT clause is added to restrict the output to 10 records for easier review.", "execution_time_ms": 5919, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	5982	success	\N	421754d1-c578-479a-ba8b-22943306c94f	0	f	2025-07-26 01:39:54.89097+00	2025-07-26 01:40:00.974737+00
