1af535fd-f6ef-4bfc-94db-1f14f7ba6eb5	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Find all agents that have been running for more than 24 hours without completing any tasks, along with their last activity time", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT ac.agent_name, ac.last_active_at FROM agent_conversations ac LEFT JOIN tasks t ON ac.id = t.agent_conversation_id WHERE ac.ended_at IS NULL AND (NOW() - ac.started_at) > INTERVAL '24 hours' AND t.id IS NULL LIMIT 100;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "1. We start by selecting the `agent_name` and `last_active_at` from the `agent_conversations` table (aliased as `ac`).  \\n2. We perform a LEFT JOIN with the `tasks` table (aliased as `t`) on the condition that the `id` of `agent_conversations` matches the `agent_conversation_id` in `tasks`. This allows us to include all agent conversations, even those without associated tasks.  \\n3. We filter the results to include only active conversations by checking that `ended_at IS NULL`.  \\n4. We also check that the difference between the current time (`NOW()`) and the `started_at` time of the conversation is greater than 24 hours using the condition `(NOW() - ac.started_at) > INTERVAL '24 hours'`.  \\n5. Additionally, we ensure that there are no tasks associated with these conversations by checking that `t.id IS NULL`.  \\n6. Finally, we limit the results to 100 entries to avoid large result sets.  \\nThis query effectively identifies agents that have been active for over 24 hours without completing any tasks, along with their last activity time.", "execution_time_ms": 6606, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	6667	success	\N	9caba184-a5b6-4871-ad0b-a2a57cc46481	0	f	2025-07-26 02:12:07.765228+00	2025-07-26 02:12:14.495996+00
