d4b254aa-c059-4540-9085-55d2baf2b9b2	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Show me a monthly trend of agent conversations by organizational type for the past 6 months, including the number of completed vs incomplete conversations", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', ac.started_at) AS month, ac.agent_type, COUNT(ac.id) AS total_conversations, SUM(CASE WHEN ac.ended_at IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS completed_conversations, SUM(CASE WHEN ac.ended_at IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS incomplete_conversations FROM agent_conversations ac WHERE ac.started_at >= NOW() - INTERVAL '6 months' GROUP BY month, ac.agent_type ORDER BY month, ac.agent_type;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "1. The query starts by selecting the month from the 'started_at' column of the 'agent_conversations' table using the DATE_TRUNC function to group the results by month. 2. It also selects the 'agent_type' to categorize the conversations. 3. The COUNT function is used to count the total number of conversations for each month and agent type. 4. The SUM function with a CASE statement is used to calculate the number of completed conversations (where 'ended_at' is not NULL) and the number of incomplete conversations (where 'ended_at' is NULL). 5. The WHERE clause filters the results to include only those conversations that started in the last 6 months. 6. The results are grouped by month and agent type to provide a breakdown of the data. 7. Finally, the results are ordered by month and agent type for better readability.", "execution_time_ms": 7806, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	7869	success	\N	7c90afb2-5164-4b7b-bfd8-6dd5af0defbd	0	f	2025-07-26 02:12:42.222413+00	2025-07-26 02:12:50.134328+00
