"493b42d6-0ef3-46d3-82fb-12c80941005e", "status": "success", "user_id": "db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7", "mcp_name": "supabase", "tool_name": "generate-sql", "created_at": "2025-07-26T00:54:46.006475+00:00", "session_id": null, "execution_time_ms": 3714, "agent_conversation_id": null}], "success": true, "row_count": 100, "is_dry_run": false, "execution_time_ms": 75, "validation_results": {"is_safe": true, "estimated_cost": "low", "security_warnings": []}}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	135	success	\N	7a4cac0f-dab6-4ab0-9265-60c0f3d2bef4	0	f	2025-07-26 02:27:04.644288+00	2025-07-26 02:27:04.787476+00
c9b0d84d-dcdc-4c2d-867b-6f070fe940ab	supabase	execute-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"sql": "SELECT status, COUNT(*) FROM mcp_executions WHERE created_at >= NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days' GROUP BY status LIMIT 10", "dry_run": false}	{"data": [{"count": 492}], "success": true, "row_count": 1, "is_dry_run": false, "execution_time_ms": 69, "validation_results": {"is_safe": true, "estimated_cost": "low", "security_warnings": []}}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	131	success	\N	92b27bcb-7b7d-479b-a83f-f594db86de5b	0	f	2025-07-26 02:29:21.304549+00	2025-07-26 02:29:21.449995+00
17e0f4db-5d42-4553-b7ec-c57abc420492	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Find users who have multiple active sessions but haven't had any task activity in the last week, ordered by their last login time", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT u.id, u.email, u.display_name, COUNT(s.id) AS session_count\\nFROM users u\\nLEFT JOIN sessions s ON u.id = s.user_id AND s.updated_at >= NOW() - INTERVAL '1 week'\\nLEFT JOIN tasks t ON u.id = t.user_id AND t.created_at >= NOW() - INTERVAL '1 week'\\nWHERE s.id IS NOT NULL\\nAND t.id IS NULL\\nGROUP BY u.id\\nHAVING COUNT(s.id) > 1\\nORDER BY MAX(s.updated_at) DESC\\nLIMIT 100;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "1. We start by selecting the user ID, email, display name, and a count of their sessions. 2. We perform a LEFT JOIN on the sessions table to include users with sessions that have been updated in the last week. 3. We also perform a LEFT JOIN on the tasks table to include users who have had task activity in the last week. 4. In the WHERE clause, we filter to ensure that we only include users who have active sessions (s.id IS NOT NULL) and no task activity (t.id IS NULL). 5. We group the results by user ID to aggregate the session counts. 6. The HAVING clause ensures we only include users with more than one active session. 7. We order the results by the last updated time of their sessions in descending order. 8. Finally, we limit the results to the top 100 users to avoid large result sets.", "execution_time_ms": 8958, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	9068	success	\N	10a43c80-9948-4b09-b051-8693a0101fe4	0	f	2025-07-26 02:19:47.315152+00	2025-07-26 02:19:56.34442+00
051414b7-26eb-496a-91f0-3c75bad24aca	supabase	get-schema	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"format": "json", "table_names": ["kpi_data", "kpi_metrics", "kpi_goals", "departments", "companies"], "refresh_cache": false}	{}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	120	error	Parameter validation failed: Parameter 'table_names' should be of type array, got object	5d427827-81d8-4f63-8079-cf23e009049f	0	f	2025-07-27 14:16:33.980345+00	2025-07-27 14:16:34.04925+00
6c0596ac-b28a-472e-9b20-fd393bfe91f9	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Calculate the cost efficiency of each agent type by dividing total successful task completions by total execution time in hours", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT ac.agent_type, COUNT(t.id) AS total_successful_tasks, SUM(me.execution_time_ms) / 3600000.0 AS total_execution_time_hours, COUNT(t.id) / (SUM(me.execution_time_ms) / 3600000.0) AS cost_efficiency FROM agent_conversations ac LEFT JOIN tasks t ON ac.id = t.agent_conversation_id AND t.status = 'successful' LEFT JOIN mcp_executions me ON ac.id = me.agent_conversation_id GROUP BY ac.agent_type ORDER BY cost_efficiency DESC;", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "1. We start by selecting the agent_type from the agent_conversations table (aliased as ac). 2. We count the number of successful tasks by joining the tasks table (aliased as t) on the agent_conversation_id, filtering for tasks where the status is 'successful'. 3. We sum the execution_time_ms from the mcp_executions table (aliased as me) for the same agent conversations. We convert this sum from milliseconds to hours by dividing by 3600000.0. 4. We calculate cost efficiency by dividing the total number of successful tasks by the total execution time in hours. 5. We group the results by agent_type to get the efficiency for each type of agent. 6. Finally, we order the results by cost_efficiency in descending order to see the most efficient agents first.", "execution_time_ms": 7031, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	7146	success	\N	3dc0b22f-e08d-44dd-aa24-642e0942afb8	0	f	2025-07-26 02:19:56.717464+00	2025-07-26 02:20:03.881824+00
30f5da01-e55c-4795-9f56-d951254b265b	supabase	execute-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"sql": "SELECT a.attname as column_name, t.typname as data_type FROM pg_class c JOIN pg_attribute a ON c.oid = a.attrelid JOIN pg_type t ON a.atttypid = t.oid WHERE c.relname = 'users' AND a.attnum > 0 AND NOT a.attisdropped ORDER BY a.attnum", "dry_run": false}	{}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	201	error	Execution failed: "failed to parse order (a.attnum.asc)" (line 1, column 3)	2f3632c8-cbd2-4884-8394-bd381571d2c3	0	f	2025-07-26 18:25:41.485026+00	2025-07-26 18:25:41.619358+00
687a0f88-3cdd-445b-876d-c03f522be98f	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Show me all companies and their departments ranked by KPI performance, including a breakdown of which specific metrics each department excels or lags in", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT c.name AS company_name, d.name AS department_name, k.metric_name, k.performance_score FROM companies c LEFT JOIN departments d ON c.id = d.company_id LEFT JOIN kpi_performance k ON d.id = k.department_id ORDER BY k.performance_score DESC", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.8, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves a list of companies along with their departments and the KPI performance metrics associated with each department. It uses LEFT JOINs to ensure that all companies and departments are included in the results, even if there are no associated KPI metrics. The query selects the company name, department name, metric name, and performance score. The results are ordered by the performance score in descending order to rank the departments based on their KPI performance.", "execution_time_ms": 5276, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	5393	success	\N	fb18ea48-37b9-4e71-bcf0-a4f1c22925aa	0	f	2025-07-26 02:20:04.284834+00	2025-07-26 02:20:09.675661+00
