7921852a-4b35-44bb-b2b9-a18b6a648e1a	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Find users who have multiple active sessions but haven't had any task activity in the last week, ordered by their last login time", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT user_id FROM sessions GROUP BY user_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1 AND user_id NOT IN (SELECT DISTINCT user_id FROM tasks WHERE created_at >= NOW() - INTERVAL '7 days') ORDER BY MAX(created_at) LIMIT 100", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query aims to find users who have multiple active sessions but have not engaged in any task activity in the last week. The logic is as follows: \\n1. We start by selecting the user_id from the sessions table and group the results by user_id. This allows us to count the number of sessions each user has. \\n2. The HAVING clause filters the grouped results to include only those users who have more than one session (COUNT(*) > 1). \\n3. We also check that the user_id is not present in the subquery that selects distinct user_ids from the tasks table where the created_at timestamp is within the last 7 days. This ensures that we only include users who have not had any task activity recently. \\n4. The ORDER BY clause is used to sort the results by the maximum created_at timestamp from the sessions table, which represents the last login time of the users. \\n5. Finally, we include a LIMIT clause to restrict the number of results returned to 100 for safety, as required by Supabase constraints. \\n\\nThis query adheres to Supabase's constraints by avoiding table aliases, column aliases, calculated fields, and complex joins, while ensuring a single ORDER BY column and including a LIMIT clause.", "execution_time_ms": 6986, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "low"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	7107	success	\N	b7c532f2-0ffb-48e2-9447-c030cef843d7	0	f	2025-07-26 02:33:05.453683+00	2025-07-26 02:33:12.559497+00
4462b977-d8a2-4299-a4e9-d0ecee6e8239	supabase	execute-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{}	{}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	105	error	Parameter validation failed: Missing required parameter: sql	88103c8a-3322-4be0-a7cc-541412f2a882	0	f	2025-07-26 19:00:09.640526+00	2025-07-26 19:00:09.706557+00
97d9a93f-8301-4e67-90ca-38cadc0cccdb	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Calculate the cost efficiency of each agent type by dividing total successful task completions by total execution time in hours", "use_context": true}	{"sql": "SELECT agent_type, COUNT(*) AS successful_tasks, SUM(execution_time_ms) / 3600000 AS total_execution_time_hours FROM tasks JOIN mcp_executions ON tasks.agent_conversation_id = mcp_executions.agent_conversation_id WHERE tasks.status = 'successful' GROUP BY agent_type LIMIT 100", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.85, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query aims to calculate the cost efficiency of each agent type by counting the number of successful tasks and summing the total execution time in hours. The query joins the 'tasks' table with the 'mcp_executions' table on the 'agent_conversation_id' column to relate tasks to their corresponding executions. It filters the tasks to only include those with a status of 'successful'. The results are grouped by 'agent_type' to aggregate the counts and sums for each type. The total execution time is calculated by summing the 'execution_time_ms' and converting it to hours by dividing by 3600000. However, this query violates Supabase constraints due to the use of calculated fields and the need for a LIMIT clause. To comply with Supabase's constraints, it is recommended to create a database view that pre-calculates the necessary fields, allowing for simpler queries without violating the constraints.", "execution_time_ms": 6376, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 0}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	6488	success	\N	a47cbb74-ca02-4812-937c-86642bc7d9d9	0	f	2025-07-26 02:33:12.905282+00	2025-07-26 02:33:19.385557+00
