2fdb17c0-8d8f-4343-b607-1a041211ff8b	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Top 5 companies by revenue in the last year", "query_type": "SELECT", "schema_tables": ["kpi_data", "companies"], "include_explanation": true}	{"sql": "SELECT companies.name, SUM(kpi_data.value) as total_revenue FROM companies JOIN departments ON companies.id = departments.company_id JOIN kpi_data ON departments.id = kpi_data.department_id JOIN kpi_metrics ON kpi_data.metric_id = kpi_metrics.id WHERE kpi_metrics.name = 'Monthly Revenue' AND kpi_data.date_recorded >= NOW() - INTERVAL '12 months' GROUP BY companies.id, companies.name ORDER BY total_revenue DESC LIMIT 5", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves the top 5 companies based on their total revenue over the last year. It starts by selecting the company names and the sum of their revenue values from the kpi_data table. The query joins the companies table with the departments table to link each company to its respective departments. It then joins the kpi_data table to access the actual revenue values recorded for each department. Additionally, it joins the kpi_metrics table to filter the results specifically for the 'Monthly Revenue' metric. The WHERE clause ensures that only records from the last 12 months are considered by checking the date_recorded field. The results are grouped by company ID and name to calculate the total revenue for each company. Finally, the results are ordered in descending order based on total revenue, and the LIMIT clause restricts the output to the top 5 companies. This query adheres to Supabase's constraints by avoiding table aliases in the SELECT clause, using full table names, and including a LIMIT clause.", "execution_time_ms": 5561, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 1}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	5