1700a408-2307-4099-88de-60783f05f4ca	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Top 5 companies by revenue in the last year", "query_type": "SELECT", "schema_tables": ["kpi_data", "companies"], "include_explanation": true}	{"sql": "SELECT companies.name, SUM(value) FROM companies JOIN departments ON companies.id = departments.company_id JOIN kpi_data ON departments.id = kpi_data.department_id JOIN kpi_metrics ON kpi_data.metric_id = kpi_metrics.id WHERE kpi_metrics.name = 'Monthly Revenue' AND kpi_data.date_recorded >= NOW() - INTERVAL '12 months' GROUP BY companies.id, companies.name ORDER BY SUM(value) DESC LIMIT 10", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves the top 5 companies by revenue over the last year. It starts by selecting the company names and the sum of their revenue values. The query joins four tables: companies, departments, kpi_data, and kpi_metrics to gather the necessary data. The WHERE clause filters the results to only include records where the metric name is 'Monthly Revenue' and the date recorded is within the last 12 months. The results are grouped by company ID and name to aggregate the revenue values. Finally, the results are ordered in descending order based on the total revenue, and a LIMIT of 10 is applied to ensure we only get the top companies. This adheres to Supabase's constraints by avoiding table aliases in the SELECT clause, using full table names, and including a LIMIT clause.", "execution_time_ms": 5264, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 1}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	5451	success	\N	1ae11a3d-b4cc-4873-b68d-73130635411f	0	f	2025-07-28 00:17:19.19481+00	2025-07-28 00:17:24.583448+00
