42e881ef-cef9-475d-8579-8991a476098c	supabase	generate-sql	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	\N	\N	{"prompt": "Top 5 companies by revenue in the last year", "query_type": "SELECT", "schema_tables": ["kpi_data", "companies"], "include_explanation": true}	{"sql": "SELECT companies.name, SUM(value) as total_revenue FROM companies JOIN departments ON companies.id = departments.company_id JOIN kpi_data ON departments.id = kpi_data.department_id JOIN kpi_metrics ON kpi_data.metric_id = kpi_metrics.id WHERE kpi_metrics.name = 'Monthly Revenue' AND kpi_data.date_recorded >= NOW() - INTERVAL '12 months' GROUP BY companies.id, companies.name ORDER BY total_revenue DESC LIMIT 5", "warnings": [], "confidence": 0.95, "model_used": "anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet", "explanation": "This query retrieves the top 5 companies by total revenue over the last year. It starts by selecting the company names and the sum of their revenue values. The query joins four tables: companies, departments, kpi_data, and kpi_metrics to gather the necessary data. The WHERE clause filters the results to only include records where the metric name is 'Monthly Revenue' and the date recorded is within the last 12 months. The results are grouped by company ID and name to aggregate the revenue correctly. Finally, the results are ordered in descending order based on total revenue, and the LIMIT clause ensures that only the top 5 companies are returned. This adheres to Supabase's constraints by avoiding table aliases in the SELECT clause and ensuring a LIMIT clause is present.", "execution_time_ms": 5338, "validation_results": {"is_valid": true, "security_issues": [], "estimated_complexity": "medium"}, "context_patterns_applied": 1}	anthropic	claude-3-5-sonnet	5439	success	\N	a635bcda-2bbf-49b0-ba0a-7b7cd652a9f4	0	f	2025-07-28 00:18:58.767893+00	2025-07-28 00:19:04.22602+00
