9d7729c1-90b7-4ea3-b208-45f48e6d2bbf	d37c1e13-9c86-4b42-8657-16a4c0df1eb1	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	executeTask	Create an invoice for TechCorp consulting services. Include 40 hours of strategic consulting at $175/hour and project documentation for $2,500 fixed fee.	{}	{"success":true,"response":"I'll assist you in creating an invoice for the consulting services provided to TechCorp. Here are the details for the invoice:\\n\\n**Invoice Details:**\\n- **Invoice Number**: INV-10238\\n- **Client**: TechCorp\\n- **Invoice Date**: January 26, 2025\\n- **Due Date**: February 10, 2025 (Net 15)\\n\\n**Services Provided:**\\n1. **Strategic Consulting**:\\n   - 40 hours at $175/hour: $7,000\\n\\n2. **Project Documentation**:\\n   - Fixed fee: $2,500\\n\\n**Total for Services**: $9,500\\n\\n**Payment Information:**\\n- **Payment Terms**: Net 15 days\\n- **Payment Methods**: ACH (preferred), Check, Wire Transfer\\n- **Late Fee**: 1.5% per month on overdue balances\\n\\nPlease review the details provided. If everything looks accurate, I can proceed with sending the invoice to TechCorp. Let me know if you need any adjustments or further information.","metadata":{"agentName":"Invoice Agent","agentType":"specialist","contextUsed":true,"contextLength":8450,"processedAt":"2025-07-29T16:02:38.985Z"}}	{"agentName": "Invoice Agent", "agentType": "specialist", "contextUsed": true, "processedAt": "2025-07-29T16:02:38.985Z", "contextLength": 8450}	completed	100	Task created, waiting for execution...	{}	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-07-29 16:02:38.985+00	300	{}	2025-07-29 16:02:35.701719+00	2025-07-29 16:02:39.105223+00	text	{}
995f2239-e93e-4676-86b1-e6a039ff39da	32cb191b-93cb-41d8-a53c-823047102593	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	executeTask	What are the pricing plans for Orchestrator AI and what do I get with each plan?	{}	{"success":true,"response":"Orchestrator AI offers three pricing plans: Starter Plan, Professional Plan, and Enterprise Plan. Here's a breakdown of each plan and what you get with it:\\n\\n1. **Starter Plan - $99/month:**\\n   - Up to 5 active agents\\n   - 10,000 interactions per month\\n   - Basic analytics and reporting\\n   - Email support\\n   - Standard AI model access\\n\\n2. **Professional Plan - $299/month:**\\n   - Up to 15 active agents\\n   - 50,000 interactions per month\\n   - Advanced analytics and custom dashboards\\n   - Priority support with phone and chat\\n   - Premium AI model access and custom training\\n\\n3. **Enterprise Plan - Custom Pricing:**\\n   - Unlimited agents and interactions\\n   - Custom integrations and development\\n   - Dedicated success manager and 24/7 support\\n   - On-premise deployment options\\n   - Advanced security and compliance features\\n\\nEach plan is designed to cater to different business needs and scales, offering a range of features and support levels. You can choose the plan that best suits your requirements and upgrade as your needs grow. If you have any specific questions or need further assistance in selecting a plan, feel free to ask!","metadata":{"agentName":"Chat Support Agent","agentType":"specialist","contextUsed":true,"contextLength":13922,"processedAt":"2025-07-29T16:33:29.668Z"}}	{"agentName": "Chat Support Agent", "agentType": "specialist", "contextUsed": true, "processedAt": "2025-07-29T16:33:29.668Z", "contextLength": 13922}	completed	100	Task created, waiting for execution...	{}	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-07-29 16:33:29.668+00	300	{}	2025-07-29 16:33:24.605093+00	2025-07-29 16:33:29.848839+00	text	{}
a3d6492f-7e7e-4aac-beb4-2b9d0f1afaae	f9cdd62e-09af-47b5-bf75-8c508d120c22	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	executeTask	Create a comprehensive Standard Operating Procedure for handling customer support tickets. Include escalation procedures, response time requirements, and quality control measures.	{}	{"success":true,"response":"**Title:** Customer Support Ticket Handling Standard Operating Procedure\\n\\n**Purpose:** \\nThis SOP aims to establish a structured process for effectively managing customer support tickets to ensure timely responses, proper escalation handling, and high-quality customer service.\\n\\n**Scope:** \\nThis procedure applies to all customer support representatives responsible for handling incoming support tickets.\\n\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n1. **Customer Support Representatives:**\\n   - Receive, assess, and respond to support tickets within the specified time frames.\\n   - Escalate tickets appropriately based on predefined criteria.\\n   - Ensure accurate and helpful responses to resolve customer issues.\\n\\n2. **Team Leads/Supervisors:**\\n   - Monitor ticket queues and response times.\\n   - Review escalated tickets for appropriate handling.\\n   - Provide guidance and support to support representatives.\\n\\n**Procedures:**\\n1. **Ticket Intake:**\\n   a. Support tickets are received through the designated ticketing system.\\n   b. Tickets are assigned to available representatives based on workload and expertise.\\n\\n2. **Response Time Requirements:**\\n   a. Initial response to a support ticket must be sent within 4 hours of receipt.\\n   b. Regular updates should be provided to the customer every 24 hours until the ticket is resolved.\\n\\n3. **Escalation Procedures:**\\n   a. Level 1 Escalation: If a ticket cannot be resolved by the initial representative, it is escalated to a senior support representative.\\n   b. Level 2 Escalation: If the issue remains unresolved or requires further expertise, it is escalated to the team lead or supervisor.\\n   c. Level 3 Escalation: For critical issues or escalations beyond the team lead's scope, the ticket is escalated to the customer support manager.\\n\\n4. **Quality Control Measures:**\\n   a. Regularly monitor support ticket responses for accuracy and professionalism.\\n   b. Conduct periodic reviews of escalated tickets to ensure proper handling and resolution.\\n   c. Implement customer feedback surveys to assess satisfaction with ticket resolutions.\\n\\n**Resources:**\\n1. Ticketing system software for ticket intake and tracking.\\n2. Knowledge base with common issue resolutions and FAQs.\\n3. Escalation matrix outlining criteria for each escalation level.\\n\\n**Quality Control:**\\nVerification steps include:\\n- Random sampling of ticket responses for quality checks.\\n- Monthly review meetings to discuss improvement areas.\\n- Metrics tracking for response times, resolution rates, and customer satisfaction.\\n\\n**Review Schedule:**\\nThis SOP should be reviewed annually or more frequently based on feedback and performance metrics. Team leads should ensure compliance with the procedures and update as necessary.\\n\\nBy following this SOP, the customer support team aims to provide efficient, effective, and high-quality support to all customers, leading to increased satisfaction and retention rates.","metadata":{"agentName":"SOP Agent","agentType":"specialist","contextUsed":true,"contextLength":6853,"processedAt":"2025-07-29T16:16:51.176Z"}}	{"agentName": "SOP Agent", "agentType": "specialist", "contextUsed": true, "processedAt": "2025-07-29T16:16:51.176Z", "contextLength": 6853}	completed	100	Task created, waiting for execution...	{}	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-07-29 16:16:51.176+00	300	{}	2025-07-29 16:16:41.163858+00	2025-07-29 16:16:51.388726+00	text	{}
