agent team", "Coordinating content creation", "Evaluating and optimizing", "Synthesizing final content", "Task execution completed"]}	completed	100	Task created, waiting for execution...	{}	{"createdAt": "2025-08-05T19:38:46.898Z", "originalLLMSelection": {"modelId": "494308ba-afb1-4bc8-983f-5acdec5920d4", "providerId": "7e157b23-07bb-47cd-9fe6-2c024d69ef6f", "temperature": 0.7, "cidafmOptions": {"customOptions": {"customModifiers": []}, "executedCommands": [], "responseModifiers": [], "activeStateModifiers": []}}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-08-05 19:39:09.488+00	300	{}	2025-08-05 19:38:47.07592+00	2025-08-05 19:39:09.951222+00	text	{}
ab9b7b22-b79a-4d39-8ad1-ab1d0fcf1474	52d6b373-7f83-4eac-b9ff-e42b7f168f29	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	executeTask	Write requirements for a simple todo list application. Include user stories, functional requirements, and technical specifications.	{}	{"success":true,"response":"# Product Requirements Document (PRD) for Simple Todo List Application\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\nThe simple todo list application aims to provide users with a user-friendly interface for creating, managing, and organizing their tasks efficiently. This application will enhance user productivity by allowing them to prioritize tasks, mark tasks as completed, and securely store task details. The key features include task creation, deletion, completion, prioritization, user authentication, data encryption, and a seamless frontend UI.\\n\\n## 2. Product Overview\\n**Goals:**  \\n- Provide users with a simple and intuitive todo list application.\\n- Improve task management and organization for users.\\n- Ensure data security and privacy through encryption techniques.\\n\\n**Objectives:**  \\n- Develop a frontend UI for task management.\\n- Implement backend server logic for task operations.\\n- Integrate user authentication and data encryption for security.\\n- Enable users to create, delete, complete, and prioritize tasks.\\n\\n**Success Metrics:**  \\n- User engagement metrics (daily active users, session duration).\\n- Task completion rate.\\n- User satisfaction through feedback and ratings.\\n\\n## 3. User Personas & Use Cases\\n**User Persona:**  \\n- **Name:** Emily\\n- **Background:** Working professional juggling multiple tasks.\\n- **Needs:** Easy task creation, clear task prioritization, secure task storage.\\n\\n**Use Cases:**  \\n1. Emily wants to create a new task with a due date.\\n2. Emily needs to mark a task as completed.\\n3. Emily wishes to prioritize tasks based on urgency.\\n4. Emily wants to delete a task that is no longer relevant.\\n\\n## 4. Functional Requirements\\n1. Task Creation:\\n   - Users can create a new task with a title, description, and due date.\\n2. Task Deletion:\\n   - Users can delete a task from the task list.\\n3. Task Completion:\\n   - Users can mark a task as completed.\\n4. Task Prioritization:\\n   - Users can prioritize tasks by setting their urgency level.\\n5. Frontend UI:\\n   - Develop a responsive and user-friendly interface for task management.\\n6. Backend Server:\\n   - Implement server-side logic for handling task operations.\\n7. Database for Task Storage:\\n   - Set up a database to store task details securely.\\n8. Task List Display:\\n   - Display all tasks in a clear and organized manner.\\n9. Task Creation Form:\\n   - Provide a form for users to input task details.\\n10. Task Detail View:\\n    - Allow users to view detailed information about a specific task.\\n11. User Authentication:\\n    - Implement a secure login system for user authentication.\\n12. Data Encryption for Task Details:\\n    - Encrypt task details to ensure data privacy and security.\\n\\n## 5. User Stories\\n1. As a user, I want to be able to create a new task with a title and due date.\\n   - **Acceptance Criteria:** Task must have a title and a valid due date.\\n   - **Workflow:** User clicks on \\"Add Task\\", fills in task details, and saves the task.\\n2. As a user, I want to mark a task as completed.\\n   - **Acceptance Criteria:** Completed tasks should be visually distinguishable.\\n   - **Workflow:** User selects a task and marks it as completed.\\n3. As a user, I want to prioritize tasks based on urgency.\\n   - **Acceptance Criteria:** Tasks should be sortable by priority level.\\n   - **Workflow:** User rearranges tasks based on priority.\\n\\n## 6. Non-Functional Requirements\\n- **Performance:** Ensure fast loading times for task lists.\\n- **Security:** Implement secure user authentication and data encryption.\\n- **Scalability:** Design the application to handle a growing number of users and tasks.\\n\\n## 7. Technical Considerations\\n- **Frontend:** Use React.js for building the frontend UI.\\n- **Backend:** Employ Node.js for server-side logic.\\n- **Database:** Utilize MongoDB for storing task details.\\n- **Security:** Implement JWT for user authentication and AES encryption for data security.\\n\\n## 8. Implementation Timeline\\n1. **Week 1-2:** Design frontend UI and task creation form.\\n2. **Week 3-4:** Develop backend server logic and database integration.\\n3. **Week 5:** Implement user authentication and data encryption.\\n4. **Week 6:** Conduct testing and bug fixing.\\n5. **Week 7:** Deploy the application for user testing.\\n\\n## 9. Success Metrics\\n- **KPIs:** Daily active users, task completion rate, user feedback ratings.\\n- **Measurement Criteria:** Increase in user engagement, positive user reviews, reduced task management time.\\n\\n## 10. Risk Assessment\\n**Challenges:**\\n- Integration issues between frontend and backend components.\\n- Ensuring data security and encryption implementation.\\n- User acceptance and adoption of the application.\\n\\n**Mitigation Strategies:**\\n- Conduct thorough testing and debugging during development.\\n- Implement security best practices and conduct security audits.\\n- Gather user feedback early on and iterate based on user preferences.\\n\\nThis Product Requirements Document outlines the key features, requirements, and considerations for the development of the simple todo list application. It serves as a roadmap for the successful implementation and launch of the product.","metadata":{"agentType":"engineering","executionType":"python_script","scriptPath":"/Users/golfergeek/projects/golfergeek/orchestrator-ai/apps/api/src/agents/actual/engineering/requirements_writer/agent-function.py","processedAt":"2025-08-06T11:36:23.673Z","method":"processTask","originalParams":{"method":"executeTask","prompt":"Write requirements for a simple todo list application. Include user stories, functional requirements, and technical specifications.","taskId":"ab9b7b22-b79a-4d39-8ad1-ab1d0fcf1474","currentUser":{"id":"db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7","email":"testuser@golfergeek.com","aud":"authenticated","role":"authenticated","appMetadata":{"provider":"email","providers":["email"]},"userMetadata":{"email_verified":true},"phone":"","emailConfirmedAt":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.570Z","confirmedAt":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.570Z","lastSignInAt":"2025-08-06T11:35:59.319Z","createdAt":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.557Z","updatedAt":"2025-08-06T11:35:59.321Z","identities":[{"identity_id":"bd517515-cb47-40de-ae10-5ac590c1c29e","id":"db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7","user_id":"db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7","identity_data":{"email":"testuser@golfergeek.com","email_verified":false,"phone_verified":false,"sub":"db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7"},"provider":"email","last_sign_in_at":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.566752Z","created_at":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.566827Z","updated_at":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.566827Z","email":"testuser@golfergeek.com"}]},"authToken":"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IkxwM1hCMXIvL0ZEQzNUSjMiLCJ0eXAiOiJKV1QifQ..LDw_mrsl1puAVG9XKYnTQlxiNhvVTCnnpwNxBZkxGW0","conversationHistory":[]},"agentName":"Requirements Writer","timestamp":"2025-08-06T11:35:59.791Z","taskId":"ab9b7b22-b79a-4d39-8ad1-ab1d0fcf1474","llmPreferences":{}}}	{"method": "processTask", "taskId": "ab9b7b22-b79a-4d39-8ad1-ab1d0fcf1474", "features": ["Task creation", "Task deletion", "Task completion", "Task prioritization", "Frontend UI", "Backend server", "Database for task storage", "Task list display", "Task creation form", "Task detail view", "User authentication", "Data encryption for task details"], "agentName": "Requirements Writer", "timestamp": "2025-08-06T11:35:59.791Z", "agent_type": "requirements_writer", "complexity": "medium", "tools_used": ["langgraph", "real-llm-calls", "modular-nodes", "state-management"], "generated_at": "2025-08-06T06:36:23.396764", "document_type": "prd", "workflow_step": "completed", "