6ddc9080-08e8-449f-afd7-d662530d80f7	5ec93fe4-ecb5-40a1-8bd2-48ed52a29413	09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b	process	I hit the ball out past the white stakes. What does that mean and what do I do?	{}	{"success":true,"message":"**🤖 Golf Rules Agent Agent**\\n\\nHitting the ball out past the white stakes means your ball is out of bounds. According to the rules of golf, you need to take a penalty stroke and play another ball from the spot where your last shot was made. This is known as \\"stroke and distance.\\" \\n\\nBe sure to check the Local Rules on your scorecard as they define the specific boundaries of the course, which may include fences, walls, white stakes, or white lines to mark out of bounds.","action":"DELEGATE","agentName":"golf_rules_agent","metadata":{"agentType":"engineering","agentName":"Rules Of Golf Agent","processedAt":"2025-08-08T15:53:09.724Z","delegatedAgent":"golf_rules_agent","delegatedAt":"2025-08-08T15:53:09.725Z","apiStatus":"executed","rawApiResponse":{"output":"Hitting the ball out past the white stakes means your ball is out of bounds. According to the rules of golf, you need to take a penalty stroke and play another ball from the spot where your last shot was made. This is known as \\"stroke and distance.\\" \\n\\nBe sure to check the Local Rules on your scorecard as they define the specific boundaries of the course, which may include fences, walls, white stakes, or white lines to mark out of bounds."},"method":"executeTask","originalParams":{"prompt":"I hit the ball out past the white stakes. What does that mean and what do I do?","userId":"09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b","conversationId":"","conversationHistory":[{"role":"assistant","content":"Hello! I'm the Specialists Manager Orchestrator. How can I help you today?","timestamp":"2025-08-08T15:52:42.997Z","metadata":{"isWelcome":true}},{"role":"user","content":"I hit the ball out past the white stakes. What does that mean and what do I do?","timestamp":"2025-08-08T15:52:50.284Z"}],"metadata":{"delegatedBy":"orchestrator","delegatedAt":"2025-08-08T15:52:56.702Z","targetAgent":"golf_rules_agent","agentType":"orchestrator","method":"processTask","agentName":"specialists_manager_orchestrator"}},"timestamp":"2025-08-08T15:52:56.703Z"},"conversationId":"","userId":"09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b"}	{}	completed	100	Task created, waiting for execution...	{}	{"createdAt": "2025-08-08T15:52:50.634Z", "originalLLMSelection": {"modelId": "494308ba-afb1-4bc8-983f-5acdec5920d4", "providerId": "7e157b23-07bb-47cd-9fe6-2c024d69ef6f", "temperature": 0.7, "cidafmOptions": {"customOptions": {"customModifiers": []}, "executedCommands": [], "responseModifiers": [], "activeStateModifiers": []}}}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	300	{}	2025-08-08 15:52:50.703076+00	2025-08-08 15:53:09.838172+00	text	{}
a25f4db6-62c9-44fd-adbe-8fb479630b8b	52d6b373-7f83-4eac-b9ff-e42b7f168f29	db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7	executeTask	Write requirements for a simple todo list application. Include user stories, functional requirements, and technical specifications.	{}	{"success":true,"response":"# Product Requirements Document (PRD) for Todo List Application\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\nThe Todo List Application is a medium complexity project aimed at providing users with a simple and efficient tool for managing their tasks. The application will allow users to create, prioritize, track completion status, and manage tasks securely. With features like user authentication, data encryption, and a user-friendly interface, the application aims to enhance productivity and organization for its users.\\n\\n## 2. Product Overview\\n\\n### Goals:\\n- Provide a user-friendly interface for task management\\n- Enable users to create, prioritize, and track task completion\\n- Ensure data security through user authentication and data encryption\\n\\n### Objectives:\\n- Develop a responsive frontend interface for seamless user interaction\\n- Implement backend server and database for storing and managing tasks\\n- Incorporate user authentication and data encryption for secure task management\\n\\n### Success Metrics:\\n- Increased user engagement and retention\\n- Decreased task completion time\\n- High user satisfaction ratings\\n\\n## 3. User Personas & Use Cases\\n\\n### User Personas:\\n1. **Busy Professional**: A working individual looking for a tool to manage daily tasks efficiently.\\n2. **Student**: A student needing to organize study tasks and assignments.\\n3. **Homemaker**: A homemaker seeking a way to manage household chores effectively.\\n\\n### Use Cases:\\n1. **Task Creation**: Users can create new tasks with titles, descriptions, and due dates.\\n2. **Task Prioritization**: Users can set task priorities to manage their workload effectively.\\n3. **Task Completion Tracking**: Users can mark tasks as complete to track their progress.\\n4. **User Authentication**: Users need to log in to access and manage their tasks securely.\\n\\n## 4. Functional Requirements\\n\\n1. **Task Management**\\n   - Create, edit, and delete tasks\\n   - Set task priorities\\n   - Mark tasks as complete\\n2. **User Authentication**\\n   - User login and registration\\n   - Password recovery option\\n3. **Data Encryption**\\n   - Encrypt task information for data security\\n4. **Database**\\n   - Store tasks with relevant details\\n5. **Backend Server**\\n   - Implement APIs for task CRUD operations\\n6. **Frontend Interface**\\n   - Design a user-friendly interface for task management\\n   - Include task list view and creation/edit forms\\n\\n## 5. User Stories\\n\\n### Story 1: Task Creation\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**: User can add a new task with a title, description, and due date.\\n- **Workflow**: User navigates to the task creation form, fills in details, and saves the task.\\n\\n### Story 2: Task Completion Tracking\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**: User can mark a task as complete.\\n- **Workflow**: User selects a task from the list view and marks it as complete.\\n\\n## 6. Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n1. **Performance**: Application should load tasks quickly and respond to user actions promptly.\\n2. **Security**: User data should be encrypted to prevent unauthorized access.\\n3. **Scalability**: System should accommodate increasing numbers of tasks and users without performance degradation.\\n\\n## 7. Technical Considerations\\n\\n1. **Frontend**: Use ReactJS for frontend development.\\n2. **Backend**: Employ Node.js for backend server implementation.\\n3. **Database**: Use MySQL for storing task data securely.\\n4. **Authentication**: Implement JWT for user authentication.\\n5. **Encryption**: Use AES encryption for securing task information.\\n\\n## 8. Implementation Timeline\\n\\n1. **Phase 1 - Planning and Design (2 weeks)**\\n   - Define project scope and requirements\\n   - Design database schema and frontend wireframes\\n2. **Phase 2 - Development (4 weeks)**\\n   - Implement frontend interface and backend server\\n   - Develop user authentication and task management features\\n3. **Phase 3 - Testing and Deployment (2 weeks)**\\n   - Conduct testing for functionality, security, and performance\\n   - Deploy application to production environment\\n\\n## 9. Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **KPIs**:\\n   - Number of active users\\n   - Average task completion time\\n   - User satisfaction ratings\\n2. **Measurement Criteria**:\\n   - Monthly active users should increase by 20%\\n   - Task completion time should decrease by 15%\\n   - User satisfaction ratings should be above 4 out of 5\\n\\n## 10. Risk Assessment\\n\\n### Potential Challenges:\\n1. **Security Vulnerabilities**: Data breaches due to inadequate encryption.\\n2. **Performance Issues**: Application slowdown with high user load.\\n3. **User Adoption**: Low user engagement leading to low retention rates.\\n\\n### Mitigation Strategies:\\n1. Regular security audits and updates to ensure data encryption strength.\\n2. Scalability testing to identify performance bottlenecks and optimize system.\\n3. User feedback collection and continuous improvement based on user needs.\\n\\n---\\nThis PRD provides a comprehensive overview of the requirements, features, and considerations for the Todo List Application, ensuring a structured approach to successful product development.","metadata":{"agentType":"engineering","executionType":"python_script","scriptPath":"/Users/golfergeek/projects/golfergeek/orchestrator-ai/apps/api/src/agents/actual/engineering/requirements_writer/agent-function.py","processedAt":"2025-08-06T11:38:34.958Z","method":"processTask","originalParams":{"method":"executeTask","prompt":"Write requirements for a simple todo list application. Include user stories, functional requirements, and technical specifications.","taskId":"a25f4db6-62c9-44fd-adb